<title>FRANCE: EU seen valuing late-Dec French wheat at $157.28.</title>
<headline>EU seen valuing late-Dec French wheat at $157.28.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-11-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>A European Union award of 311,300 tonnes of free-market soft wheat at a maximum refund of some 16.5 Ecus per tonne values a tonne of late-December French wheat at $157.28 per tonne, Reuters calculates.</p>
<p>The figure, which should be regarded as an estimate only, is based on benchmark standard-quality French milling wheat at Rouen and may vary significantly for other EU origins and types.  </p>
<p>The calculation uses the following assumptions gathered from market sources and Reuters data.</p>
<p>    Rouen-delivered soft wheat (Dec)   850.00 francs/tonne</p>
<p>    Carrying charge (2nd-half Dec)	36.36 francs/tonne</p>
<p>    Fob charges/other charges	     27.50 francs/tonne</p>
<p>    EU refund				   16.50 ecus/tonne</p>
<p>     + EU increment (added to refund)    1.10 ecus/tonne</p>
<p>   = Subsidy (at 6.61023 green rate) 116.34 francs/tonne</p>
<p>    One-month forward dollar/franc     5.0706 francs/dollar</p>
<p>    Implied fob price in dollars	 157.28 dollars/tonne.</p>
<p>The same formula suggests an unsubsidised French fob price of $180.23 per tonne.</p>
<p>--Paris newsroom +331 4221 5146</p>
